{
  "_about": "The North American theme's palettes (issue M2-12, PRD \"Art direction\"): soft colours for each family of buildings, as sRGB hex. A building picks its wall, roof and trim colours from its type's family, by its id (render/building-tint.ts), so the same building has the same colours for every player and after every reload. `types` names each building type's family, by its id in the sim's buildings.json. `fixed` holds the colours no building tints: the glass of skylights, the tints a window's glass takes, one per building, the sky the glass reflects, the blinds behind it, and paving. The glass is kept well lighter and bluer than the roads (issue #137), whose asphalt it was once mistaken for. Presentation, not balance: no prices and no source years.",
